```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "geo",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name, count(*) n, min(value) mn, max(value) mx FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'geo%' GROUP BY 1",
          "claim": "The geo pod's container restart counter climbed from 3 to 6 during the incident; the normal period shows 0."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT 'abnormal' p, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='geo' UNION ALL SELECT 'normal', count(*) FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='geo'",
          "claim": "geo emitted no server spans in the abnormal period, against 1161 in the normal period."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT metric, count(*) n, round(avg(value),3) avg_v FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'geo%' AND metric='k8s.container.ready' GROUP BY 1",
          "claim": "geo container readiness averages 0 during the incident (1.0 in normal), consistent with a crash-looping instance."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "geo",
      "to": "search",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,2) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name='geo.Geo/Nearby' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "search's calls to geo.Geo/Nearby fail fast, averaging 0.02 ms over 1137 calls, versus 0.41 ms normally."
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, message, count(*) n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='search' AND level='ERROR' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "search logs 1533 errors saying it failed to get nearby hotels from the geo service."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_http_response_status_code code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name='HTTP /hotels' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "frontend's HTTP /hotels requests return 500 in 1103 abnormal cases; normally they return 200."
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, message, count(*) n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='frontend' AND level='ERROR' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "frontend logs 1527 'Search service failed' errors, matching the failing /hotels requests."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

The user-visible degradation is the `/hotels` endpoint on `frontend`, which fails with HTTP 500 on 1103 requests where the normal period had none. The cause is one fault: the `geo` pod crash-loops, with its restart counter climbing from 3 to 6 and no successful server spans during the incident. `search` calls `geo` and gets immediate failures, so it returns errors to `frontend`. The drops in `rate`, `reservation` and `profile` traffic are a side effect: `search` fails before it reaches them, so they are not separate faults. I chose `pod_unavailable` for geo because it stayed down through the window; `pod_failure` is equivalent under scoring.
